# Brute Force Approach

For every character in `s`

Search for an unused matching character in `t`.

```text
a

↓

search

↓

n

↓

search

↓

a

↓

...
```

This repeatedly scans the second string.

---

## Java Code

```java
class Solution {

    public boolean isAnagram(String s, String t) {

        if (s.length() != t.length()) {
            return false;
        }

        boolean[] used = new boolean[t.length()];

        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {

            boolean found = false;

            for (int j = 0; j < t.length(); j++) {

                if (!used[j] && s.charAt(i) == t.charAt(j)) {

                    used[j] = true;
                    found = true;
                    break;
                }

            }

            if (!found) {
                return false;
            }

        }

        return true;
    }
}
```

---

## Complexity

| Time | Space |
|------|-------|
| O(N²) | O(N) |

Too slow for large strings.

