# Even Better — Frequency Array

Interviewers often ask:

> The input contains only lowercase English letters.

In this case, a `HashMap` is unnecessary.

There are only **26 possible characters**.

We can directly index into an array.

---

## Idea

```text
count['a']++

count['b']++

...

Process second string

count['a']--

count['b']--
```

If every count is zero,

the strings are anagrams.

---

# Production-Grade Java (Optimal)

```java
class Solution {

    public boolean isAnagram(String s, String t) {

        if (s.length() != t.length()) {
            return false;
        }

        int[] count = new int[26];

        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {

            count[s.charAt(i) - 'a']++;
            count[t.charAt(i) - 'a']--;

        }

        for (int value : count) {

            if (value != 0) {
                return false;
            }

        }

        return true;
    }
}
```

This is the solution expected when the character set is known.

